    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0232" n="1066" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1066"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10406</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-10T13:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 10, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 11, 3 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2704. War Trade Board [from Frothingham]:</p>
                <p>No. 1639. Fuller. Your 1274, Department’s 1626, September 26. Action in
                    Portuguese matter has been delayed by lack of reply from French Minister of
                    Blockade and have telegraphed Stetson in Paris to press the matter in view of
                    peace overtures from Berlin. Feeling here is that every effort should be made to
                    speed up liquidation of enemy firms in Allied countries. Proposed withdrawal of
                    stat[utory] list Portugal should be accelerated if at that price more rapid
                    liquidation enemy firms could be secured.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d187-f1"/>
                    Frothingham.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d187-f1" n="1" xml:id="d187-f1-content">
                <p>Last sentence is as corrected by telegram No. 2837 from Great Britain, received
                    October 17 (File No. 763.72112/10463).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
